    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 The membership tier is derived at read time. I added a GOLD rule that takes precedence over SILVER/BRONZE:\n   - `membershipTier(owner)` now returns `GOLD` first when `isGoldHousehold(owner)` is true, then falls back to the existing SILVER (no namesakes + email present) and BRONZE rules.\n   - `isGoldHousehold(owner)` counts all owners sharing the same non-blank `householdId` (via `clinicService.findAllOwners()`) and returns true when that count is \u2265 3 (`GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (and updated its description) so the generated `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum.GOLD` constant exists.\n\n**How it satisfies the spec:** Household membership is keyed on `householdId`, which the create flow (`applyHousehold`) assigns to every owner in a shared household when `sharesHousehold=true`. Since the tier is computed on each `GET`, the third opt-in member's household reaches 3 members and all members read back as `GOLD`; households below 3 keep the existing BRONZE/SILVER behavior.",
